\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O Ye who taste that love is sweet,
\par Set waymarks for all doubtful feet
\par The stumble on in search of it.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Sing notes of love: that some who hear
\par Fear off, inert, may lend an ear,
\par Rise up and wonder and draw near.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Lead lives of love; that others who
\par Behold your life may kindle too
\par With love, and cast their lot with you.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

